---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Privacy policy for my private dashboard (dashboard.danielsohel.com). Google requires a public
// policy at a stable URL before the dashboard's Google sign-in can be published.
const updated = '9 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy · Sohel Danial" description="Privacy policy for Daniel's Dashboard, a private personal dashboard.">
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24 [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:text-lg [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-fg [&_li]:ms-5 [&_li]:list-disc [&_ul]:space-y-2 [&_p]:mt-3">
		<a href="/" class="font-mono text-sm text-accent hover:underline">← danielsohel.com</a>
		<h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg">Privacy policy</h1>
		<p class="text-sm text-dim">Last updated: {updated}</p>

		<p>
			This policy covers "Daniel's Dashboard" (the "app"), a private personal dashboard run by Sohel Danial (Daniel Sohel) at
			dashboard.danielsohel.com. The app has a single user: me. It is not offered to the public, and no one else can sign up or
			connect an account.
		</p>

		<h2>What Google data the app accesses</h2>
		<p>When I connect my own Google account, the app requests these permissions:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<span class="text-fg">Gmail</span> (gmail.modify): to list, read, search and show my emails; to send emails I write and
				explicitly send; and to archive, label, mark as read/unread or move emails to the trash when I choose to.
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="text-fg">Google Calendar</span> (calendar): to show my calendars and events, and to create, change or delete
				events when I choose to.
			</li>
			<li><span class="text-fg">Basic profile</span> (openid, email, profile): to confirm that the connected Google account is mine.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>The app can also connect my university mailbox (Microsoft 365) in the same way, for the same purposes.</p>

		<h2>How the data is used</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Email and calendar data is used only to show it to me inside the app and to carry out actions I ask for.</li>
			<li>
				When I use the built-in AI assistant, the parts of my data needed to answer my request (for example, the emails or events I
				ask about) are sent to Anthropic's Claude API to generate the answer. Anthropic processes this data as a service provider
				under its commercial terms and does not use it to train its models. Nothing is sent to Anthropic unless I use the assistant or
				the "My day" summary.
			</li>
			<li>The AI assistant cannot send email on its own: it can only prepare drafts, which are sent only when I click Send.</li>
			<li>Google user data is not sold, not used for advertising, and not shared with anyone else.</li>
			<li>No one other than me reads the data.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Storage and security</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				The app runs on a computer in my home and is reachable only through an encrypted Cloudflare Tunnel, protected by Cloudflare
				Access and a password login.
			</li>
			<li>
				Access tokens are stored encrypted. Email and calendar content is fetched when needed and is not copied into a separate
				database, except for drafts and chat history I create in the app.
			</li>
			<li>Encrypted backups of the app's database are kept for about 30 days.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
		<p>
			Daniel's Dashboard's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any other app will adhere to the{' '}
			<a class="link" href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
				>Google API Services User Data Policy</a
			>, including the Limited Use requirements.
		</p>

		<h2>Removing access and deleting data</h2>
		<p>
			Access can be removed at any time in the app's Settings ("Disconnect") or at{' '}
			<a class="link" href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
			Disconnecting deletes the stored tokens. Chat history and drafts can be deleted in the app.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>Questions: <a class="link" href="mailto:daniel@danielsohel.com">daniel@danielsohel.com</a></p>
	</main>
</Base>
